R.append({'quantity':'Q16: matched-beam 4-3/3-2 and 3-2/2-1 brightness-temperature ratios at N, S and Bridge, beam-mismatch test and N-S-Bridge contrast significance',
 'target':'N, S, Bridge positions; HCN and HCO+; common beams Xb4f native 5.72x3.54" PA82 (J=3,4) and Xb55 native 8.64x6.00" (J=2,3,4); circular 6.5 and 10" for the mismatch test',
 'value':'T43/T32 in the Xb4f native beam (response of the other nucleus 0.003): HCN N 0.450+-0.006, S 0.357+-0.011, Bridge 0.362+-0.008; HCO+ N 0.565+-0.005, S 0.486+-0.005, Bridge 0.494+-0.004. Xb55 beam (response 0.13): HCN N 0.382, S 0.308, Bridge 0.347; HCO+ 0.494, 0.438, 0.475; T32/T21 (Xb55 beam) HCN N 0.419, S 0.377, Bridge 0.402; HCO+ 0.523, 0.498, 0.521. Contrasts (HCN; Xb4f beam / Xb55 / circular 6.5" / circular 10"): N/S 1.26 / 1.24 / 1.16 / 1.06; N/Bridge 1.25 / 1.10 / 1.09 / 1.03; S/Bridge 0.99 / 0.89 / 0.94 / 0.97. HCO+: N/S 1.16 / 1.13 / 1.10 / 1.04; S/Bridge 0.98 / 0.92 / 0.93 / 0.96. Significance with systematics (stat; Q12 differential recovery +-0.05; J4-J3 registration 0.2" rms scaled from the 0.5" shift test): HCN N/S = 1.26 +- 0.04 (stat) +- 0.09 (total) = 2.9 sigma; HCO+ N/S 1.16 +- 0.08 = 2.0 sigma; HCN N/Bridge 1.25 +- 0.13 (2.0 sigma); S/Bridge 0.99 +- 0.11 (HCN), 0.98 +- 0.07 (HCO+): S is NOT distinguishable from the Bridge in this diagnostic; the distinct object is N (modestly: 2-3 sigma). Beam checks: exact common-beam convolution verified (Xb47 4.14x2.70 PA87 -> 5.720x3.540 PA82.0 and 8.640x6.000 PA90.0, peaks 1.000); J4-J3 centroid offsets of the N and S peaks <= 0.21" (HCN N +0.21" north, S -0.06"; HCO+ 0.19/0.09"); shifting the J4 map by 0.5" changes T43/T32 by <=0.04 (N), 0.03 (S), 0.07 (Bridge) HCN. Absolute 10% per-band calibration enters the individual ratios (14%; used in the RADEX errors) and cancels in the contrasts. Smaller/larger beams only dilute the contrast, so 1.26 (HCN) is a lower bound on the intrinsic N/S ladder contrast for these two regions.',
 'uncertainty':'stat 0.005-0.011 per ratio; contrast total (stat+recovery 0.05+registration) +-0.09 HCN, +-0.08 HCO+; calibration 14% on single ratios','unit':'ratio of RJ brightness temperatures','assumptions':common,'confidence':'medium',
 'evidence':'s72_q16_native_beams.py -> out/q16/s72.txt; s76_q16_maps.py (convolution self-test) and s82_q16_beamtests.py -> out/q16b/s82.txt/json. Position read = bilinear value at the Xb4d peak positions; J4 map from Xb47 convolved to the Xb4f beam.'})
R.append({'quantity':'Q16: can the S-nucleus core T43/T32 be measured from the 6" data? Origin of the 0.06-0.09 offset of the p0012 core ladders (re-implemented deblend, factorial test, injection-recovery, forward-model ratio field)',
 'target':'S and N nucleus core T43/T32 (HCN, HCO+) at the Xb4f beam from Xb4d 3-2 templates; team-a p0012 values HCN N 0.395 S 0.268; HCO+ N 0.482 S 0.442',
 'value':'(1) A p0012-like NNLS template deblend (N, S, Bridge [, Outer] templates from Xb4d 3-2, same template for 3-2 and 4-3, Xb4f beam; s77, s80) reproduces the p0012 values only in part and unstably: HCN N 0.32-0.42, S 0.23-0.30 (median over core radius 1-2", fit radius 10/14", no Outer; baseline none/plane; formal vs empirical errors), HCO+ N 0.39-0.53, S 0.35-0.48, Bridge 0.29-0.58; with an Outer component the cores jump (HCN S 0.28-0.58, HCO+ S 0.54-0.87) because the Outer J=3 amplitude collapses to ~0 (degenerate). The fits are statistically unacceptable with formal errors (chi2/dof 20-300): the moment-0 maps have negative bowls of -0.5 to -1.2 Jy/beam km/s and an empirical off-source rms 0.6 (HCN)/1.0 (HCO+) vs formal 0.25, and clipping the noisy Xb4d template at zero adds a +0.5-2 Jy/beam km/s positive bias after convolution to 5.7x3.5". (2) Injection-recovery (s79; truth = observed J3 map, J4 = known ratio field times the Xb4d template plus an extended term, correlated noise 0.3, 20 realisations): when the model assumptions hold the deblend is nearly unbiased: input S 0.36 -> 0.346 [0.305,0.370]; 0.268 -> 0.283; 0.45 -> 0.407; extended gas poor in J4 (halo 0.20): 0.36 -> 0.299 (bias -0.06, worst case); N recovered within 0.045 (low). So NNLS positivity/window by themselves do not produce a -0.09 offset; the real J4 map departs from a J3-shaped template (ratio gradients, different Xb47/Xb4f filtering of extended gas). (3) Forward-model ratio field (s78; J3 reproduced exactly, J4 = conv(template x rho(x)) + rho_h R, rho = rho_h + core excesses of width s, errors with the empirical floor, chi2~dof): rho_S = 0.19-0.72 (HCN) depending on s=1-3" and on the template (HCN or HCO+ morphology), rho_h = 0.0-0.2: the S core ladder is NOT measurable at this resolution (model-dependent over a factor 2-3), consistent with Q3/p0011. (4) Bounds (s85): only 0.31-0.45 (r<1-1.5") to 0.65 (r<2.5") of the S 3-2 flux in the Xb4f beam is compact-core (Xb4d template) and 55-70% is non-core; if all non-core gas has T43/T32 <= the N value (0.45 HCN, 0.57 HCO+) the S core is >= 0.27 (HCN, rc 1.5") / 0.41 (HCO+), i.e. p0012 S 0.268 is at the edge of the allowed range for HCN. p0012 own components predict an S aperture ratio of 0.27-0.33 (HCN) and 0.35-0.46 (HCO+) versus the observed 0.357+-0.011 and 0.486+-0.005: shortfall 0.03-0.09 (HCN), 0.03-0.13 (HCO+); the p0012 S core value requires the non-core gas around S (50-60% of its flux) to have T43/T32 >= 0.43 (N-like), higher than p0012 own Bridge (0.363) and Outer (0.28). Subtracting Bridge-like gas (ladder 0.362) at 10-30% share changes the S core by <0.01 (HCN 0.357 -> 0.355) because the Bridge ladder equals the S ladder; subtracting N-like gas (0.450) at 30% (unphysical share: N response 0.003) gives 0.317 (HCN), 0.452 (HCO+). Net: S core T43/T32 (HCN) = 0.36 (+0.09,-0.09), not measured; the p0012 value 0.268 is not excluded but is not supported either; origin of the offset: not a single choice (baseline bowl, template clipping and Outer degeneracy each move S by 0.03-0.3).',
 'uncertainty':'S core T43/T32 (HCN) 0.27-0.45 allowed; injection scatter +-0.03, bias -0.01..-0.06 under ideal assumptions; model-dependent range 0.19-0.72 in the ratio-field fit','unit':'ratio of RJ brightness temperatures',
 'assumptions':common+[A('templates','Xb4d 3-2 0.94x0.74" moment-0 (HCN or HCO+), >4 sigma pixels (or clipped at 0 for the p0012-like variant); recovery of Xb4d relative to Xb4f 0.77-0.91 at the peaks (Q12)'),A('baseline','plane fitted in an annulus 12-22" of both coarse maps (or none)'),A('errors','moment-0 formal 0.25 or empirical off-source 0.6/1.0 Jy/beam km/s, +5% model floor')],'confidence':'medium',
 'evidence':'s77_q16_deblend_repro.py -> out/q16b/s77.txt; s80_q16_deblend_factorial.py -> out/q16b/s80.txt/json; s78_q16_ratiofield.py -> out/q16b/s78.txt; s79_q16_injection.py -> out/q16b/s79.txt; s85_q16_convex_bound.py -> out/q16b/s85.txt. team-a deblend script is not in the snapshot (only the csv), so the exact p0012 recipe could not be re-run.'})
R.append({'quantity':'Q16: S and N Tkin from the p0012 RADEX fit with ladder-pair swaps, decontaminated and recovery-corrected ladders, Tbg 2.73 and 5 K (profile dchi2(T))',
 'target':'S and N nuclei; p0012 joint 8-datum non-LTE fit re-run with perturbed ladders (R32, R10, 3-2/1-0 kept as in p0012)',
 'value':'S, Tbg 2.73 K, dchi2 relative to each minimum [min at; allowed dchi2<4; dchi2(20), (80), (100)]: p0012 core vector 0.268/0.442 [30 K; 10-50 K; 0.9, 9.3, 14.4]; only the 3-2/2-1 pair swapped to apertures [30 K; 20-40 K; 0.2, 10.5, 14.2] (does NOT relax the exclusion: this pair is not the driver); only the 4-3/3-2 pair swapped [40 K; 30-65 K; 8.0, 4.1, 7.3] (this pair drives it); both pairs at aperture values [65 K; 25-80 K; 4.9, 2.7, 4.5]; aperture + Q12 recovery (x1.07, x1.11) [40 K; 30-80 K; 6.5, 1.4, 4.8]; Bridge-like subtraction 10/30% [65 K; 25-80 K; 4.7/4.3, 2.9/3.2, 4.5/4.5]; N-like subtraction 10/20/30% (bounding, unphysical shares) [20-80/20-65/20-65 K; dchi2(80) 3.2/4.2/6.5, (100) 4.9/5.9/8.2]; N-like 30% + recovery [15-80 K; 2.5, 5.7]; bracket (mean of aperture and N-like 30%, error with half the range, recovery) [25-80 K; 1.9, 5.2]. Tbg 5 K: p0012 vector dchi2(80)=11.2, (100)=19.4 (allowed 20-40 K); aperture 3.1/8.9 (20-80 K); aperture+recovery 0.9/7.0; bracket 1.5/8.6 (20-80 K); N-like 30% 9.0/14.2 (20-40 K). N, Tbg 2.73 K: p0012 vector min chi2 19.3 (poor) at 30 K, allowed 25-100 K; aperture min 9.1 at 100 K, allowed 65-150 K, dchi2(30)=6.0, (20)=12.4; aperture+recovery allowed 65-150 K, dchi2(30)=9.4 (Tbg 5 K: 14.7 at 20 K). RESULT: the p0012 statement that Tk(S)>=80 K is excluded (dchi2 9-14) is not robust: with any ladder vector inside the allowed range of the S core, S Tk is 25-80 K at dchi2<4 and 80/100 K are disfavoured at only dchi2=1.4-6.5 / 4.5-8.2 (1.2-2.5 / 2.1-2.9 sigma); the hot exclusion needs the 0.268 core value. The statement S<50 K survives only for that vector. N is hotter than 30 K at 2.5-3 sigma (aperture ladders), N Tk 65-150 K, with the p0012 N core vector fitting poorly.',
 'uncertainty':'11-point T grid (15-30% steps above 40 K); one-zone model; Tbg 2.73-5 K','unit':'K',
 'assumptions':common+[A('ladder vectors','aperture = matched-beam ladders of s72 (3% template error added to the 14% scale error); contaminant subtraction rho_core=(rho_ap - w rho_c)/(1-w), w = share of the lower-J flux')],'confidence':'medium',
 'evidence':'s81_q16_Sfit_decon.py -> out/q16b/s81_{base,tbg5}.csv/.log; s84_q16_summary_table.py -> out/q16b/s84.txt (all numbers); round-1 s73/s74 -> out/q16/s74.txt (leave-one-out, 25% errors, Tbg 10 K disfavoured for both nuclei)'})
R.append({'quantity':'Q16: excitation contrast of N, S and Bridge as (Tk ratio, n ratio) from the matched-beam HCN+HCO+ ladders (Bridge as control)',
 'target':'N, S, Bridge; 4 ladders each (HCN, HCO+ 3-2/2-1 in the Xb55 beam and 4-3/3-2 in the Xb4f beam), p0012 RADEX classes A+B+F2 pooled, flat T 10-150 K and log n priors, Tbg 2.73 K',
 'value':'Marginal Tk (16/50/84%): N 40/65/100 K, S 25/40/65 K, Bridge 30/50/80 K (log n 4.4-5.25 for all three, prior-dominated; n(H,O mean) median 4.75). P(Tk>=80 K): N 0.40, S 0.10, Bridge 0.23. Pairwise (regions independent): Tk_N/Tk_S median 1.60 [0.80,2.67], P(Tk_N>Tk_S)=0.67, P(ratio>1.4)=0.53; n_N/n_S median 1.0 [0.32,3.2], P(n_N>n_S)=0.45, P(either Tk ratio>1.4 or n ratio>2)=0.75; Tk_N/Tk_Bridge 1.25 [0.62,2.3] (P>1 0.55); Tk_S/Tk_Bridge 0.80 [0.46,1.6] (P>1 0.30; n ratio 1.33 [0.3,4.2]). With Q12 recovery corrections: Tk N 40/80/100, S 30/50/80, Bridge 30/65/100 K; Tk_N/Tk_S median 1.33 [0.65,2.7], P(Tk_N>Tk_S)=0.62. So the measured N-S ladder contrast (HCN 4-3/3-2 1.26, 2-3 sigma) cannot be turned into a significant Tk or n difference with these four ladders: it allows Tk_N/Tk_S ~1-2.7 or n_N/n_S ~1-3 along the usual Tk-n degeneracy, with equal probability for n higher and Tk higher (P(Tk ratio>1 and n ratio<1)=0.39). S and Bridge are statistically identical (S/Bridge ladder ratios 0.99+-0.11 HCN, 0.98+-0.07 HCO+); N is the only region with a (modestly) different ladder: N distinct from S and Bridge at 2-3 sigma in the ratio, but not in (Tk, n).',
 'uncertainty':'posteriors on an 11-point T and coarse n grid; regions treated as independent (shared calibration/recovery systematics ignored; the recovery variant brackets them)','unit':'K; ratio','assumptions':common+[A('data used','4 ladders only; R32 and 1-0 data (not available for the Bridge) switched off for all three regions as a control')],'confidence':'medium',
 'evidence':'s83_q16_contrast.py -> out/q16b/s83.txt/json'})
R.extend(keep)
d['interpretation']=d['interpretation'].rstrip()+(' Q16 (p0012 S-nucleus temperature, round 2): the p0012 result that S is cool (20-30 K) with >=80 K excluded (dchi2 9-14) is NOT supported. It rests on the deblended S-core 4-3/3-2 ladders (HCN 0.268), a quantity the 6" data cannot measure: our re-implemented deblends give 0.23-0.58 depending on baseline, template and component choices, a forward-model ratio-field fit gives 0.19-0.72, and injection-recovery shows the method is nearly unbiased only when its assumptions hold. The matched-beam S aperture (0.357) is dominated (55-70%) by non-core gas, and p0012 own components under-predict it by 0.03-0.09 (HCN). Using any ladder vector inside the allowed range, S has Tk 25-80 K and 80/100 K are disfavoured at only dchi2 1.4-6.5 / 4.5-8.2; the hot exclusion and S<50 K are not robust. What does survive is a modest excitation contrast: T43/T32 N/S = 1.26+-0.09 (HCN, 2.9 sigma) and 1.16+-0.08 (HCO+, 2.0 sigma) in the matched 5.7x3.5" beam, N distinct from the Bridge (1.25+-0.13) while S is not distinguishable from the Bridge (0.99+-0.11, 0.98+-0.07). The contrast corresponds to Tk_N/Tk_S >~1 (median 1.3-1.6) or n_N/n_S up to ~3 along the Tk-n degeneracy, neither significant; p0011 and p0012 do not conflict (p0011 used circular 6.5/10" apertures that mix N and S, p0012 deblended). Absolute Tk: N 65-150 K, S and Bridge 25-100 K (one-zone, Tbg 2.7-5 K).')
d['caveats'].append('Q16: aperture ladders are not core ladders (the S aperture contains Bridge-like gas and the outflow lobe, 55-70% non-core flux); the S Tk range 25-100 K spans the p0012 core vector, the aperture and the contaminant-subtracted vectors. p0012 deblend script is not in the snapshot, so its exact recipe was not re-run (our re-implementation reproduces it only in part and unstably). Different spatial filtering of Xb47 and Xb4f (Q12: T43/T32 true/obs 1.03-1.12) is applied only as a variant. Moment-0 maps carry negative bowls and an off-source rms 2.5-4x the formal noise; the T grid is coarse (15-30% above 40 K). One-zone RADEX, Tbg blackbody (Tbg 10 K disfavoured, 5 K tested), no IR pumping (HCN 3-2/1-0 failure from Q3/Q4), CO and Tdust not measured. A resolved J=4 (or 2-1) map at ~1" would settle the S core ladder; the archive has none.')
json.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=1)
print(len(R),'results')
